sequenceDiagram

  actor CL as ZAS clinician
  participant HIX as Chipsoft HIX
  participant ENT as Microsoft Entra ID
  participant IDB as Identity broker
  participant BFF as Professional BFF
  participant AME as Access Management Engine
  participant CORE as Core service
  participant LUI as Luscii integration layer
  participant LUS as Luscii (professional tools)
  participant EVE as Event Bus

  autonumber

  Note over CL,EVE: ZAS clinician launches the platform from HiX via SMART on FHIR<br/>(Pathway Orchestrator embedded view and Luscii professional tools embedded view)

  CL->>HIX: Login (Entra ID SSO + MFA already established)
  CL->>HIX: Open patient record
  CL->>HIX: Click "Open Carepath Platform" tab<br/>(SMART launch button)

  HIX->>BFF: SMART launch URL<br/>?iss=⟨HiX FHIR base⟩&launch=⟨opaque token⟩
  BFF->>HIX: GET /.well-known/smart-configuration<br/>(SMART discovery)
  HIX-->>BFF: SMART config (authorize_endpoint, token_endpoint)

  BFF->>HIX: GET /authorize<br/>?launch=⟨token⟩&scope=launch patient/*.read user/*.read<br/>&aud=⟨HiX FHIR base⟩
  BFF->>EVE: Log Authorization Request

  HIX->>ENT: Validate clinician session<br/>(OIDC, SSO + MFA)
  ENT-->>HIX: User identity (clinician UPN)
  HIX-->>BFF: Authorization code

  BFF->>HIX: POST /token<br/>(code, client_id, code_verifier)
  HIX-->>BFF: Access token<br/>+ id_token + launch context<br/>(patient ID, encounter ID, user)

  BFF->>IDB: Validate id_token<br/>map clinician UPN → platform user
  IDB->>ENT: SCIM lookup (group memberships)<br/>(if not yet cached)
  ENT-->>IDB: Groups (specialism, role)
  IDB-->>BFF: Validated identity + role claims

  BFF->>AME: Resolve entitlements<br/>(user, patient context, encounter)
  AME->>CORE: Therapeutic-relationship check<br/>+ specialism + campus + erkenning
  CORE->>EVE: Log therapeutic-relationship check
  CORE-->>AME: Pathway access scope
  AME-->>BFF: Active role = ZAS clinician<br/>+ scoped pathway IDs

  BFF->>CORE: GET pathway state for patient
  CORE->>EVE: Log access pathway request

    CORE->>LUI: GET actions<br>for patient
    LUI->>LUS: Query professional view data
    LUS-->>LUI: Alerts, trends, measurements
    LUI-->>CORE: Clinical signal payload

  CORE-->>BFF: Pathway timeline, pending tasks,<br>signals, IC status
  BFF-->>CL: Render embedded view in HiX<br/>(iframe with launch context preserved)
  Note over CL, EVE: Clinician sees: Patient Carepath<br>Both in HiX patient context, no second login.



  Note over CL,EVE: SMART launch capability on the HiX side is owned by ZAS/Chipsoft.<br/>Newwave Care configures the platform side and validates the integration.